;; cljfmt configuration for the clojure-paredit fixture.
;;
;; Plan 062b's expected-output drift caveat (see
;; docs/work/changelog/062b-clojure-deferred-slices.org) was about
;; the fixture inheriting a user-side cljfmt config; pinning the
;; configuration here side-steps that risk and lets the L3
;; format-buffer scenarios assert a single deterministic shape.
;;
;; cljfmt is conservative by default: it leaves multi-space gaps
;; between symbols (`(defn  weird-spacing', `( *   x    x)') alone
;; because collapsing them is treated as too aggressive for the
;; default profile.  The L3 scenario in
;; `tests/scenarios/l3-batch-clojure-lsp-format.el' wants the
;; aggressive shape so the post-format buffer is fully canonical
;; (no internal whitespace residue), which matches the user's
;; on-keystroke expectation for `C-c l = ='.  Enabling
;; :remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? gives that.
;;
;; clojure-lsp picks this file up via its `:cljfmt-config-path'
;; setting (default `.cljfmt.edn').  The file is intentionally
;; tracked (the fixture's `.gitignore' does not list `.cljfmt.edn')
;; so a fresh clone reproduces the same format-buffer outcome.
{:remove-multiple-non-indenting-spaces? true}
